{
 "meta": {
  "slot_model": "FIVE SLOTS PER CHARACTER: offensive, defensive1 (Auras — universal), defensive2 (class-locked: Tunics/Epidermides/Lockpicks/Oven Mitts), defensive3 (Colours — universal), special (Days — universal). Offensive is class-locked: Bats/Symbols/Star Charts/Dessert Molds. Matches the canon equip screen.",
  "acquisition_design": "Per GM ruling: Symbols and Epidermides are SINGLE-COPY SHARED POOLS across the three ring-bearers — their difficulty is allocation. Purifier, Bandit, and Burnt pieces are individual hunts — their difficulty is exploration. Universal pools (Auras, Colours, Days) are single-copy across all six.",
  "stat_model": "GEAR IS ADDITIVE, per GM ruling. The level tables are the true base stats; equipment adds its values on top, full stop. Piece magnitudes are sized at ~15% of checkpoint stats per tier (T5 20%), so a fully-geared character runs up to ~15% above the printed tables. The bestiary was derived against table values — if geared parties make fights run easy, that is rebalanced GM-side with GM tools (waves, template edits, income bands), never by reducing player stats. There is no base-stat discount anywhere in the engine.",
  "invented": "Star Charts, Lockpicks (Bandit), Dessert Molds, Oven Mitts (Burnt) — the four cells canon leaves empty; names GM-renameable.",
  "unassigned_canon_pool": [
   "Left Glove",
   "Right Glove",
   "Starred Shorts",
   "Nerves of Steel",
   "Lucky Coin — Boxxer/Ballman prize items, GM uniques (bestiary: Ballman fight rewards)"
  ],
  "source": "OFF_2008.xml Items page x canon equip screen x off-level-tables.json",
  "slot_restrictions": "SLOT-FIRST EQUIP FLOW: editing gear starts from the slot, not the inventory. Click a slot and the picker shows ONLY that slot's legal items — defensive1 shows Auras, defensive2 shows the character's personal category (Tunics / Epidermides / Lockpicks / Oven Mitts), defensive3 shows Colours, special shows Days, offensive shows the class weapon category — filtered further to unequipped copies (shared pools: an item worn by another ring-bearer appears greyed with the wearer's name, selectable only after they unequip). Illegal equips are unrepresentable in the UI, so no refusal message ever fires; the server still validates category-slot match as the authoritative backstop against malformed requests, per the server-authoritative rule. The category field \"slot\" drives both the filter and the validation.",
  "gear_effect_vocabulary": "Gear effects are ACTIVE, per GM ruling: inert effects are incoherent in engine-resolved combat (the engine would apply the crit and the GM would have to hand-correct mid-tempo). All effects use existing systems only. Vocabulary: crit_immune (wearer cannot receive crits — Negative Space machinery); status_immune:[...] (Strong immunity while worn); res_vs:{status:N} (+N effective RES vs that status); cp_cost_mult (multiplies competence CP costs); overworld_tick_immune (negates the per-transition poison tick damage; the status itself persists); attack_element (wearer’s BASIC ATTACKS carry this element, competences unchanged — same forcing as the Purifier’s Runs); hits (basic attack resolves N times); flat stat riders. RESTAT INTERPRETATIONS flagged for GM veto: canon \"Special\" attribute = Sugar; Perfect Symbol’s dual attribute resolves at the better multiplier vs the target (the one micro-rule added); Wednesday’s terrain protection = the overworld poison tick (distinct from Sunday, which blocks the status); Thursday/Friday riders restatted to +2 ATK / +2 ESP with res_vs 30/50. Supply control is GM placement: Days are GM-priced treasures, T5s are superboss drops. An effect inexpressible in this vocabulary gets flagged to the GM, never half-built."
 },
